Day 15 – Multi-Table JOINs (Patients × Staff × Services Weekly)
21 Days SQL Challenge – Indian Data Club
Overview

In Day 15, the goal was to understand how to perform multi-table joins between:

patients

staff

services_weekly

Since staff_schedule does not exist in this dataset, all reports were built using the available schema.

This day focuses on understanding how multiple tables can be connected to produce analytical reports—a key skill in SQL-based data analytics.

Topics Covered

INNER JOIN vs LEFT JOIN usage

Mapping patients to staff based on service

Creating multi-table hospital analytics

Aggregation using COUNT(), GROUP BY

Handling missing data gracefully

Practice Questions & Solutions
1. Join patients with staff to display the staff handling each service
SELECT 
    p.patient_id,
    p.name AS patient_name,
    p.service AS patient_service,
    s.staff_name,
    s.role
FROM patients p
JOIN staff s 
      ON p.service = s.service;

2. Combine services_weekly with staff to show staff assignment counts
SELECT 
    sw.week,
    sw.service,
    sw.patients_admitted,
    sw.patients_refused,
    COUNT(s.staff_id) AS staff_assigned
FROM services_weekly sw
LEFT JOIN staff s 
       ON sw.service = s.service
GROUP BY 
    sw.week, sw.service, 
    sw.patients_admitted, sw.patients_refused;

3. Generate a full hospital operations report (patients + weekly data + staff)
SELECT 
    p.patient_id,
    p.name AS patient_name,
    p.service,
    sw.week,
    sw.patients_admitted,
    sw.patients_refused,
    s.staff_name,
    s.role
FROM patients p
LEFT JOIN services_weekly sw 
       ON p.service = sw.service
LEFT JOIN staff s
       ON p.service = s.service
ORDER BY sw.week, p.service;

Daily Challenge
Service Analysis Report for Week 20

Required output:

service name

total patients admitted

total patients refused

average patient satisfaction

staff assigned count

staff present (NULL because no staff_schedule table)

SELECT 
    sw.service,
    sw.patients_admitted AS total_patients_admitted,
    sw.patients_refused AS total_patients_refused,
    sw.patient_satisfaction AS avg_patient_satisfaction,
    COUNT(s.staff_id) AS staff_assigned,
    NULL AS staff_present
FROM services_weekly sw
LEFT JOIN staff s 
       ON sw.service = s.service
WHERE sw.week = 20
GROUP BY 
    sw.service,
    sw.patients_admitted,
    sw.patients_refused,
    sw.patient_satisfaction
ORDER BY total_patients_admitted DESC;

